	(text "DS12885 CLOCK, CALENDAR AND NVRAM ON A JUMPER-PICKED PORT PAIR" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "965c712b-5cb2-5f1a-b7bb-6a7cc708e958"))
	(text "U13 DS12885+ (Ken, 2026-11-18): Intel timing (MOT low), RESET high, CS = SEL_UART (low: the clock is the chip the\naddress port's byte picked; sheet Serial port); Y1 32.768 kHz, 6 pF; BT1 a CR2032 in a\nflat holder, on VBAT. JP4 picks the ports: address on 2, 4 or 6, data on 3, 5 or 7 (set to 6/7); its last row puts IRQ\non -INT (off). OSTB_L = NAND(MRD_H, TPB) (U6D): TPB of a read. OUT address: AS = NOR(select, OSTB_L) (U12A); OUT\ndata: R/W = NOT NOR(select, OSTB_L) (U12B, U12C); INP data: DS = NOT NOR(select, MRD_H) (U12D, U5C). RN1 pulls the\nselects and IRQ up. JP5: a shunt grounds RCLR, which clears the 114 bytes of RAM (not the clock) while the chip runs\nfrom its battery, the power off; open, nothing changes (RCLR has its own pull-up: no outside one)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f2bd9624-4364-5c4f-bf93-91fe215c87a9"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
